Original papers in Experimental Economics (project=='ee') average 28.00 pages (median 27.5, sd 7.37, n=18 unique originals from 2011-2014). Original papers in Psychology (project=='rpp') average 11.01 pages (median 9.0, sd 6.21, n=88 unique originals from 2008-2015). Within Psychology, Social originals (n=46) average 11.70 pages (median 9.5) and Cognitive originals (n=42) average 10.26 pages (median 8.0); both sub-disciplines remain below the Experimental Economics mean. Sensitivity checks confirm the gap: including rows with the drop quality flag raises the rpp mean to 11.23 (n=95 unique originals), and using the row-level sample (no de-duplication of repeat replication pairs) gives 11.00 pages for rpp (n rows=90); ee is unchanged across all scenarios because no ee row carries the drop flag and no ee original is repeated.